@startuml 04-sequence-task-lifecycle
title FlowAI Platform - Task Lifecycle (sequence) - Router is the queue manager

autonumber

participant "Source" as Src
participant "Operator (UI)" as U
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "State Registry" as StateRegistry
participant "Secret Registry" as SecretRegistry
participant "Router" as Router
participant "Executor" as EX
participant "Agent Container" as AG
participant "LLM Provider" as LLM

note over Src, U
  Router is the task queue manager. It holds the incoming
  queue, the executor wait list, and the executor pool.
  Router is NOT connected to GW, StateRegistry, or SecretRegistry - those are
  independent services in the operator-facing graph.
  Auto submits to Router directly. EX registers + pulls
  from Router. EX writes historical events directly to State Registry.
end note

== Submit (source publishes to Router) ==

Src -> Router : REST POST /tasks with bearer_token, prompt, tools, secret_ids
Router -> Router : Enqueue in incoming list
Router -> Router : Process via services (validation, scope binding)
Router -> Router : Move to executor wait list
Router --> Src : 202 task_id

U -> GW : WS connect with bearer_token (subscribe to historical events)
GW -> GW : Validate bearer_token
GW -> StateRegistry : REST subscribe (read) - WS subscribes to State Registry events
StateRegistry -> GW : subscription ack
GW -> U : WS upgrade ack

== Executor registration (on startup) ==

EX -> Router : REST POST /executors with routing_target, capacity, metadata
Router -> Router : Register executor X with capacity N
Router -> Router : Initialize slots_in_use = 0
Router --> EX : 201 with executor_id

== Executor ready signal ==

EX -> Router : REST POST /executors/:id/ready
Router -> Router : Mark executor as having N free slots

== Executor pulls task (the dispatch loop) ==

EX -> Router : REST GET /tasks/next (with routing_target)
Router -> Router : Match: pending task + EX with routing_target matches, slots_in_use less than capacity
Router -> Router : slots_in_use = slots_in_use plus 1
Router --> EX : 200 with task_spec, scope_token (delivered from Router's wait list)

note over EX
  EX receives full task payload from Router.
  EX is in the data plane at task execution time.
end note

EX -> SecretRegistry : REST open env with scope_token
SecretRegistry --> EX : env-style keys
EX -> EX : Pull pre-built agent image (OCI) if not cached
EX -> EX : Prepare a new container runtime
EX -> AG : Start container, mount secrets

note over AG, EX
  Agent is a black box. Runs initial instructions.
end note

AG -> LLM : Prompt + history
LLM --> AG : Completion or tool_use

== Agent loop (historical events go to State Registry, status goes to Router) ==

loop agent loop
  AG --> EX : stdout (event stream)
  EX -> StateRegistry : REST POST /events with task_id, kind, payload
  EX -> Router : REST POST /tasks/:id/status with status update

  opt Operator intervenes
    U -> GW : inject message / cancel / rerun (WS frame, bearer_token)
    GW -> GW : Validate bearer_token
    GW -> StateRegistry : REST POST /control-requests with task_id, action, payload
    StateRegistry -> StateRegistry : Append control request and audit entry
    EX -> StateRegistry : REST GET pending control requests for task_id
    StateRegistry --> EX : pending control request
    EX --> AG : apply control to task runtime
  end

  AG -> LLM : Next prompt
  LLM --> AG : Next completion
end

== Finalize ==

AG --> EX : final result (stdout / exit code)
EX -> Router : REST POST /tasks/:id/status with status=terminal, result
Router -> Router : Mark task done in wait list; slots_in_use = slots_in_use minus 1
EX -> StateRegistry : REST POST /events with status=terminal, result (historical)

== Executor returns to pool ==

EX -> Router : REST POST /executors/:id/ready
Router -> Router : Mark executor as having at least one free slot

note over AG, EX
  Container terminated. Scope token expires.
end note

@enduml
